# OksaSDR tour, "The app's own": beat cancel (BC) on a phone frequency, USB with the 2.9 kHz
# receive filter (the user: phone always with 2.9 kHz). A 41 m broadcast carrier on 7.335,
# 1 kHz off the dial, stands in for someone tuning up. Receive only; BC put back off.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # The app's own
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption Beat cancel (BC), the app's own, not in SmartSDR. In a phone QSO someone tunes up on your frequency: a steady whistle over the voice, worst in headphones. A broadcast carrier 1 kHz off the dial stands in for him here.
freq 7.334
span 10
wait 1000
caption !mark 560,115
mode USB
wait 2500
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 1500
taptext 2.9k
wait 1500
close
wait 4000
caption Tap the DSP flags, then BC: it finds the steady carrier and notches it out within 0.15 s; the voice stays.
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 2000
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 9000
caption BC off: the whistle is back. Up to four carriers at a time, in the voice modes.
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 5000
close
wait 1000
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
